    "notes": "1. Total Revenue is constructed as the sum of all revenue line items, including both noninterest revenue and net interest income. The primary statement shows 'Total net revenue' as a subtotal, but the schema requires the full composition. Therefore, the components of Noninterest revenue and the components of Net interest income (Interest income and Interest expense) are listed individually. Interest expense is included as a negative component within total_revenue to arrive at Net interest income. 2. Total Operating Cost includes all operating expenses from the income statement: Provision for credit losses and all components of Noninterest expense (Compensation, Occupancy, Technology, Professional, Marketing, Other). This aligns with standard banking industry practice. 3. Taxes and Interest expenses are mapped directly from 'Income tax expense' and 'Interest expense'. Per rule 13, the sign convention for these fields is the opposite of the income statement presentation: items that reduce income are positive. Therefore, the positive values from the statement for these expenses are reported as positive numbers. 4. Numbers in parentheses in the source are treated as negative values. 5. All values are in millions (scale 1E6) and currency is USD.",
